## 5. Panel 3 — Triggered Alert Systems

```
⚠ Triggered Alert Systems
[AIR QUALITY]  [WATER SUPPLY]
```

Or when nothing is triggered:
```
✓ All systems nominal. No active alerts.
```

### How are triggered systems determined?

**On the backend** (`cascadeEngine.js`):
```javascript
const CRISIS_THRESHOLD = 0.60;

if (aqi_risk   >= 0.60) → 'AIR_QUALITY'
if (water_risk >= 0.60) → 'WATER_SUPPLY'
if (health_risk>= 0.60) → 'PUBLIC_HEALTH'
if (traffic_risk>=0.60) → 'TRAFFIC_NETWORK'
```

**On the frontend** (`Dashboard.tsx`), this is **re-derived** after the city multiplier is applied, using the same 0.60 threshold:

```typescript
const CRISIS_THRESHOLD = 0.60;
const scaledAqiRisk = Math.min(scaledCascade.aqi_impact / 500, 1);

if (scaledAqiRisk           >= CRISIS_THRESHOLD) → 'AIR_QUALITY'
if (scaledCascade.water_stress >= CRISIS_THRESHOLD) → 'WATER_SUPPLY'
if (scaledCascade.health_risk  >= CRISIS_THRESHOLD) → 'PUBLIC_HEALTH'
if (scaledCascade.traffic_disruption >= CRISIS_THRESHOLD) → 'TRAFFIC_NETWORK'
```

> The frontend re-derives triggered systems **because the city multiplier can push a value above 0.60 even if the backend didn't trigger it** — ensuring the displayed alerts match the scaled values shown in the cards.

> **❌ No ML.** Pure threshold comparison on cascade outputs.

