## 7. Panel 5 — 7-Day Urban Crisis Trend Chart

```
7-Day Urban Crisis Trend               [WORSENING]

   AQI ── Risk Score % ── Water Quality ─ ─ Traffic ─ ─
200│                                    ⚠ Crisis 60%
150│          ●──●──●──●──●──●
100│  ●──●
   └──────────────────────────────────────────────────
   May 17  May 18  May 19  May 20  May 21  May 22  May 23
```

### How this chart is built

**Function called:** `getHistoryRaw(city.id)` → `GET /history?cityId=bengaluru`

**Backend `history.js` runs a MongoDB aggregation pipeline:**

```javascript
[
  { $match: { cityId: "bengaluru" } },
  {
    $group: {
      _id: { cityId, year, month, day },   // group by day
      latestRecord: { $last: "$$ROOT" },    // keep the newest reading per day
      date: { $first: "$date" }
    }
  },
  { $sort: { year: -1, month: -1, day: -1 } },  // newest first
  { $limit: 7 },                                  // last 7 days
  { $replaceRoot: { newRoot: "$latestRecord" } }  // flatten
]
```

**Then for each day record:**
```javascript
const riskResult = computeRisk(rec, heatwaveLevel);  // ← cascade engine
risk_scores.push(riskResult.risk_score);
```

**So the chart gets:**
```
labels:          ["May 17", "May 18", ..., "May 23"]
aqi:             [145, 152, 158, 165, 170, 175, 178]
water_quality:   [78, 76, 75, 74, 73, 72, 72]
traffic:         [55, 58, 60, 62, 63, 65, 65]
risk_scores:     [0.28, 0.31, 0.33, 0.36, 0.38, 0.41, 0.42]
```

**Dashboard transforms for chart:**
```typescript
risk_pct = risk_scores[i] × city.riskMultiplier × 100
// e.g. 0.42 × 1.0 × 100 = 42.0
```

### Trend Direction label

Computed in `history.js`:
```javascript
const delta = lastRisk - firstRisk;

if (Math.abs(delta) < 0.05) → 'STABLE'
if (delta > 0)              → 'WORSENING'
if (delta < 0)              → 'IMPROVING'
```

The label (`WORSENING` / `IMPROVING` / `STABLE`) appears as a colored badge beside the chart title.

### Chart lines and axes

| Line | Color | Y-Axis | Data |
|------|-------|--------|------|
| AQI | 🟠 Orange | Left (raw values) | `aqi` |
| Risk Score % | 🔴 Red | Right (0–100%) | `risk_pct` |
| Water Quality | 🔵 Blue dashed | Left | `water_quality` |
| Traffic Density | 🟣 Purple dashed | Left | `traffic` |

**Reference line:** A dashed red line at `60%` on the right Y-axis marks the **crisis threshold** — the point where the cascade engine starts triggering alert systems.

> **❌ No ML.** Chart data is computed by the cascade engine applied to each historical MongoDB record.

