## 10. Does the Dashboard Use ML?

| Panel | Uses ML? | Reason |
|-------|---------|--------|
| Risk Score (Panel 1) | ❌ No | Cascade engine formula |
| AQI Card (Panel 2) | ❌ No | Raw MongoDB reading |
| Water Stress Card | ❌ No | Cascade propagation formula |
| Health Risk Card | ❌ No | Cascade propagation formula |
| Traffic Card | ❌ No | Normalized sensor value |
| Triggered Systems (Panel 3) | ❌ No | Threshold comparison on cascade output |
| Sensor Readings (Panel 4) | ❌ No | Direct MongoDB values |
| 7-Day Chart (Panel 5) | ❌ No | Cascade engine on historical records |
| WebSocket live updates | ❌ No | Cascade engine on simulated sensor data |

> **The dashboard page does NOT use any ML model.**
> 
> The Python ML service (Prophet + XGBoost) is used **only** in:
> - **Forecast page** (`/app/forecast`) — 7-day AQI + water predictions
> - **Simulate → Compare** — ML forecast per scenario  
> - **Transparency page** — SHAP feature importance

